From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omarchy Ferrix <maintainers@omarchy.invalid>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:18:15 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] exynos-modem: add an explicit google-kleaf-cpif kernel
 backend

Google's Kleaf CPIF module (radio/samsung/s5300 a8976934) exposes the
same /dev/umts_boot0 boot node as the radio-first s5300_modem driver, but
three operations differ:

- IOCTL_POWER_RESET is _IOW('o', 0x21, struct boot_mode) and takes a
  pointer, not the integer _IO('o', 0x21). Map Cold -> NORMAL, Dump ->
  DUMP and Warm -> SILENT by kernel action.
- IOCTL_GET_SRINFO is _IO('o', 0x45) with the record inline after a u32
  size. Implement that layout and keep the crash-reason dump-boot
  disabled on CPIF, because its start_dump_boot effects are unreviewed.
- ipc_read() returns 0 after a 100 ms empty wait. Gate OEM reads on
  poll(POLLIN), treat a 0-byte read as no data, and end the session only
  on POLLHUP/POLLERR, so the handle (and the kernel rx queue) is kept.

The backend is selected only by --kernel-backend google-kleaf-cpif. On it
the channel nodes are fixed to umts_boot0, umts_rfs0 and oem_ipc1, and any
other path is refused before a node is opened. --print-config prints the
resolved configuration without opening anything. The default
linux-google-tegu-wwan backend keeps the upstream behaviour.
